From: NeoDCT build
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: raise minimum required from 3.4 to 3.5

libvncserver 0.9.14 declares cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.4). CMake 4.0
removed compatibility with a minimum below 3.5 and aborts at configure:

    Compatibility with CMake < 3.5 has been removed from CMake.

A host with CMake >= 4 (current Arch, among others) therefore cannot build
this package at all. 3.5 is a floor the project's CMakeLists already satisfies
-- nothing in it uses a pre-3.5 behaviour -- so the bump is mechanical and
changes no build logic. Upstream has not tagged a release with the fix.

Signed-off-by: NeoDCT build <noreply@neodct>
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
-cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.4)
+cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.5)
 
 project(LibVNCServer VERSION 0.9.14 LANGUAGES C)
 include(CheckFunctionExists)
